From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Scott Jordan <scott@spaceshipcreative.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 05:03:40 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 03/25] [Platform][CUDA] Disable PDL on SM12x (GB10)

CudaPlatformBase.is_arch_support_pdl() returned `major >= 9`, so GB10
(compute capability 12.1) launched the mamba/KDA state Triton kernels
(causal_conv1d, gather_initial_states, scatter_states) and the mHC
TileLang kernels with programmatic dependent launch. On GB10 this races
in the KDA state and mHC kernels for GLM-5.3-Flash. Return False for
major == 12; Hopper (9), datacenter Blackwell (10) and SM11x keep PDL.

All PDL users in the tree read this predicate (the mHC kernels cache it
at import), so no other call sites change. vLLM has no general PDL
env-var override (only the LoRA-specific VLLM_LORA_DISABLE_PDL), so none
is added.

From MiaAI-Lab glm53-flash_SM121.py, bake_pdl_off_sm12 (MIT,
Copyright (c) 2026 MiaAI-Lab); same idea, narrowed to exclude only
major 12 (MiaAI's version returns `major in (9, 10)`).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 vllm/platforms/cuda.py | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/vllm/platforms/cuda.py b/vllm/platforms/cuda.py
index 68c3aa785..ba333d53f 100644
--- a/vllm/platforms/cuda.py
+++ b/vllm/platforms/cuda.py
@@ -758,7 +758,9 @@ class CudaPlatformBase(Platform):
             major, _ = torch.cuda.get_device_capability(device)
         except Exception:
             return False
-        return major >= 9
+        # PDL is unvalidated on SM12x (GB10, RTX 50xx) and races in the KDA
+        # state and mHC kernels on GB10, so keep it off there.
+        return major >= 9 and major != 12
 
 
 # NVML utils
